description: P10.6/#43 represent a defrecord instance as a map carrying :lw/type (D122: the backend has no type kind), so (dissoc r :a) keeps the tag where native returns a plain map, (= r {:a 1}) is false where native compares fields, and pr-str shows the tag. The jank suite shows it in dissoc.cljc and the record tests. Fixing it is a representation decision (a map kind that carries its type out of band, or a type kind) and touches the runtime layout under discussion on PR #25, so it waits for that answer. Out of scope for the 2026-10-15 loop.

